---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ObfuscatedEmail from "../../components/ObfuscatedEmail.astro";
// screening@avainrva.com confirmed live (Protonmail via Cloudflare) — see ObfuscatedEmail.astro
// for the click-to-reveal technique that replaces the old WP anti-spam plugin.
---
<BaseLayout title="Contact / Screening" description="How to reach Ava Celeste, and what screening requires.">
  <section>
    <h1>RSVP!</h1>
    <p class="drop-cap">
      Have you read the <a href="/you/client-guide/">client guide</a> yet? If you have, then this step
      should be a breeze for you. Even if you haven't, just follow my lead. It's really not hard to do,
      and you impress me by doing so.
    </p>
    <p>
      Contacting me within the same 24hrs you want to meet isn't going to work out. I check email once
      per day, and Sundays I try to be 100% offline.
    </p>
    <p>RS2K members are welcome.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>1. Screen first, deposit second</h2>
    <p>
      If you pass screening and we mutually agree on a date/time, I'll send you a few simple options,
      including crypto, for paying the deposit.
    </p>
    <p class="callout">
      Please be aware: if you have a Hotmail/Outlook or Comcast account, Microsoft and Comcast have
      blacklisted my email address. You'll need a different email address if you'd like to get a reply.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. Double confirmation</h2>
    <p>
      After confirming receipt of your deposit, I'll contact you to confirm the booking the morning of
      or night before. After receiving your confirmation, I'll send the necessary final details (i.e. my
      phone number, clothing description, etc.).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. Any questions?</h2>
    <p>If you still have questions, they're likely answered in the <a href="/you/client-guide/">Client Guide</a>. I'm thorough, but as concise as possible.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What I need to verify your employment</h2>
    <p>One of the following:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A publicly-accessible link to a company website with a page about you</li>
      <li>Articles or interviews featuring you</li>
      <li>LinkedIn profile with 500+ connections and headshot</li>
      <li>Any other online, publicly-accessible source featuring your full name and current employment, with or without a photo</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you can't find yourself easily via Googling the information you've given me, I won't be able to either.</p>
    <p class="note">
      You can always send me a simple greeting as a way of letting me see your LinkedIn profile. I will
      not follow or interact with your profile.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>If you're not on LinkedIn</h2>
    <p>The frustration-reducing alternative screening option:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>$50</li>
      <li>An unobstructed photo of the front of your state ID</li>
      <li>A professional screener will screen you</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      They have access to databases I do not, and can screen you with less reliance on the lazy DIY
      methods I use. I still need your employment information, though — that's still required, for
      reasons I cover in the Client Guide.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Screening via email</h2>
    <p>
      For several reasons, I'm going form-free. The screening information I request is the same, with or
      without a form. Email is not a way to avoid screening.
    </p>
    <p class="callout">
      Please be aware: if you have a Hotmail/Outlook or Comcast account, Microsoft and Comcast have
      blacklisted my email address. You'll need a different email address if you'd like to get a reply.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Your screening information:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your full name, and city/state of residence [+ RS2K phone number, if you're a member]</li>
      <li>The full name of your company (if self-employed, the full name of your company/DBA)</li>
      <li>A direct link to online proof of employment (as detailed above)</li>
      <li>Preferred day and time to meet, and for how long</li>
      <li>Please introduce yourself. What would you like me to know about you, as a person?</li>
    </ul>
    <ObfuscatedEmail user="screening" domain="avainrva.com" />
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <h2>Thank you!</h2>
    <p>I look forward to hearing from you, and meeting you, soon.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .callout {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent-gold);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .note { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .cta { text-align: center; margin-top: 2rem; }
</style>
